.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PCID 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pcid
.Nd PCI configuration-space enumerator and the pci: scheme
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/pcid
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the ACPI boot blob, locates the MCFG table and maps the first 1 MiB of the
ECAM window.  It scans bus 0, records the vendor, device, class, revision and six
32-bit BAR values of every function, prints
.Dq pcid: devices= Ns Ar count
and registers the
.Dq pci:
scheme.
.Pp
Enumeration is limited to bus 0 in this milestone.  The server receives the
RootDevice capability through the
.Ql root
service grant; it is the only process allowed to create
.Dv MmioRegion
objects.
.Pp
The scheme layout is:
.Bl -tag -width Pa -compact
.It Pa /
one packed K60 directory entry per function, named
.Sy bb:ss.f
.Pq bus, slot, function in lowercase hex .
.It Pa /bb:ss.f/info
the 40-byte little-endian device record: bus, slot, function, class, subclass,
programming interface, revision, vendor, device, six BAR words, the interrupt
line and the interrupt pin.
.It Pa /bb:ss.f/bar Ns Ar n
opens a fresh
.Dv MmioRegion
for that 32-bit or 64-bit memory BAR and returns it as an S25 attachment.  The
region covers the whole BAR, sized by writing all ones into the BAR register
and reading the mask back during enumeration (the original value is restored
immediately).  I/O BARs and absent BARs return
.Er ENOENT .
.It Pa /bb:ss.f/bars
one
.Ql index kind size
line per BAR
.Pq kind is Ql memory , Ql io or Ql absent ,
so a launcher can choose a BAR and tell its driver the length.
.It Pa /bb:ss.f/config
opens a fresh
.Dv MmioRegion
over that function's 4 KiB configuration page and returns it as an S25
attachment, for capability discovery through
.Xr raven-driver 3 .
.El
.Pp
Only read access is accepted for the informational files; every open of a
BAR or configuration page is a new attachment and the client owns the returned
handle.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/pcid.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/pcid.toml
service manifest with the
.Ql root
grant
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr svcd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
server first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
